@* Exercise 073 - Virtualize Items Provider (advanced).
   Goal:   Feed a list that is far too long to render from a paged source, one
           window at a time.
   Drills: <Virtualize> with an ItemsProvider, the StartIndex/Count of an
           ItemsProviderRequest, and ItemsProviderResult<T> carrying the total the
           component sizes itself by.
   Passes: dotnet test --filter FullyQualifiedName~Ex073_ *@

@* TODO: render a <Virtualize> over an items provider:
     - its ItemContent is <div class="row">…</div> holding the item's text;
     - each rendered item comes from Provider, never from a list this component
       materialised itself. *@

@code {
    /// The paged source. StartIndex/Count of the request say which window is wanted;
    /// the result carries the items plus how many there are in total.
    [Parameter] public Func<ItemsProviderRequest, ValueTask<ItemsProviderResult<string>>> Provider { get; set; }
        = _ => ValueTask.FromResult(new ItemsProviderResult<string>([], 0));

    [Parameter] public float ItemSize { get; set; } = 20f;

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
        => throw new NotImplementedException("TODO: Ex073 - render the virtualized list");
}
